@startuml SSD-S4-handle-shortfall
' System sequence diagram for UC-06 Handle shortfall, slice S4
' Black-box view: actor, system, system events and returned outcomes only
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

title SSD-S4 Handle shortfall (UC-06)

actor "Hub staff member\n(or manager)" as A
participant ":KerryHubSystem" as S

A -> S : viewShortfalls(orderId)
alt order found and actor permitted
  S --> A : ShortfallView (per short line: requested, allocated,\n outstanding, accepts reduced, accepts removal, permitted substitutes)
else actor is a volunteer (1a)
  S --> A : Failure(NOT_PERMITTED)
else order does not exist (1b)
  S --> A : Failure(NOT_FOUND)
end

loop for each short line to resolve
  A -> S : resolveShortfall(orderLineId, resolution: ShortfallResolutionType,\n  substituteProductId [0..1])
  alt valid and permitted
    S --> A : ShortfallResolutionResult (allocations made,\n remaining shortfall, contact required)
  else actor is a volunteer (1a)
    S --> A : Failure(NOT_PERMITTED)
  else order line does not exist (3a)
    S --> A : Failure(NOT_FOUND)
  else no outstanding shortfall, already resolved, or removal with allocations (3b, 5b)
    S --> A : Failure(INVALID_STATE)
  else preferences do not permit the resolution (4a, 4b)
    S --> A : Failure(NOT_PERMITTED)
  end
end

note over A, S
  viewShortfalls only reads data, so it has no operation contract.
  resolveShortfall changes state: contract OC-07.
  A substitute with too little stock is a success with a remaining shortfall (5a).
end note
@enduml